<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TAOM enlistment service-issue armor rosters (#375 Phase 4).

  Roster ID convention: enlist_{runtimeCultureId}_{rank}, rank in
  recruit|soldier|veteran|sergeant. Armor slots ONLY (Head/Body/Leg/Gloves/Cape);
  no gender dimension. Issued to the party INVENTORY (not equipped) once per rank
  by EnlistmentEquipmentService; fallback chain exact -> lower ranks ->
  enlist_default_{rank} -> none (EnlistmentRosterResolver).

  RUNTIME culture ids (the #1 TAOM data bug; lore names are WRONG here):
  vlandia=Rohan, empire=Dunland, aserai=Harad, khuzait=Rhun, sturgia=Dale,
  battania=Khand, lothlorien=Galadhrim.

  lothlorien and battania define no troops_*.xml file of their OWN, but both bind
  to another culture's tree, so they are NOT rosterless: taom_spcultures.xml gives
  lothlorien basic_troop=imladris_recruit / elite_basic_troop=imladris_infantry,
  i.e. the same Rivendell tree rivendell itself uses; spcultures.xslt gives
  battania (Variag/Khand) basic_troop=loke_rim_initiate /
  elite_basic_troop=loke_rim_cavalry, i.e. khuzait's Rhun tree. Their rosters
  therefore mirror rivendell and khuzait rank-for-rank (the generator's
  TREE_ALIASES map reproduces them). enlist_default_{rank} stays the fallback for
  any culture that really has neither.

  GENERATED by tools/generate_enlistment_rosters.py from per-culture donor troops
  (rank -> level band per derive_armor_tiers.level_to_tier) + the live
  LOTRLOME_Armory index. Hand-tune freely, then keep re-runs append-only with the
  seed-missing flag; a full apply regeneration overwrites tuned culture rosters.
  (XML comments cannot contain double hyphens, hence the spelled-out flag names.)
  The enlist_default_{rank} block is hand-authored and survives regeneration.
-->
